# Every systemd unit on THIS computer that writes rt/lowcmd (G1D) or
# rt/arm_sdk (G1), one per line. Install as /etc/g1/actuator-writer-units.
#
# Each unit listed here should run the writer check as ExecStartPre with
# --self set to its own name (see deploy/g1-guardian.service). A unit then
# refuses to start while any other listed unit is running. Nothing is ever
# stopped by the check.
#
# Check the real unit names on the robot first, e.g.
#   systemctl list-unit-files --type=service | grep -Ei 'guardian|lowcmd|arm|fatigue|executor'
# and keep this file in step with what is installed.

# --- G1D body computer (where the guardian runs) ---
g1-guardian.service
# Unitree-side 250 Hz lowcmd publisher (workspace question Q16b: is it still enabled?)
fatigue.service
# Refactor stage-B executor services, if installed here: add their real names.

# --- Box (a separate file on that computer) ---
# The refactor task node writes rt/lowcmd with --arm-backend dds (its default).
# vision-arm-control-refactor.service
